  "referenceVersion": "1-draft",
  "scope": "The 66-book Luther 1545 numbering represented by the LUTH1545STR Zefania edition dated 2009-01-20. This is an explicit edition profile, not an alias for all German Bibles or all Luther revisions. Apocrypha and other edition layouts have not been verified.",
  "dataLicense": "CC0-1.0",
  "evidence": {
    "sourceEdition": {
      "identifier": "LUTH1545STR",
      "date": "2009-01-20",
      "filename": "SF_2009-01-20_GER_LUTH1545STR_(LUTHER 1545 MIT STRONGS).xml",
      "sha256": "b1140f1eab996c88456ec035d69fee96d4cd279abbffa9dc602f44dbf2ed90f7",
      "textSource": "http://www.luther-bibel-1545.de/",
      "strongsSource": "http://www.winbibel.de/de/lutherstrong/lu1545adds.htm"
    },
    "reference": "Bundled BOSReference 1-draft; compared with local OET-LV original-numbered text and the unfoldingWord Hebrew/Greek texts.",
    "corroboration": "https://github.com/crosswire/jsword/blob/master/src/main/resources/org/crosswire/jsword/versification/Luther.properties",
    "method": "Chapter/verse inventory checked in all 66 books. Luther follows the reference Hebrew/Greek numbering, with the explicit boundary and ordering exceptions below. CrossWire corroborates the general numbering tradition; its rules are not imported, and its different NUM 25, CH1 12, PSA 13 and REV 12 inventory is not substituted for this edition. Strong tags were used only to locate candidates: several tags in this edition are offset from their actual German words, so annotations do not establish the verse boundaries.",
    "identityChecks": [
      "GEN 32:1 and EXO 7:26: cross-chapter English shifts already represented by eng.",
      "SA1 20:42/21:1, KI1 22:43/44 and ISA 63:19: Hebrew divisions retained.",
      "PSA 3, 51, 54, 64, 127: numbered titles/combined title-and-body follow the reference; PSA 13 needs the explicit split below.",
      "JOL 3/4 and MAL 3:19-24: Hebrew chapter divisions retained.",
      "MAT 7:1: judgement saying; ACT 19:40 includes the dismissal; CO2 13:12 includes both greetings; JN3 1:14-15 separates final greetings, all agreeing with the reference."
    ],
    "exceptions": [
      "NUM 25:18 ends with the plague transition (und die Plage danach kam); reference 25:19 has that transition separately. Luther 26:1 starts the divine speech, without that transition.",
      "KI2 15:38 has Jotham death/burial; 15:39 has Ahaz succession, both in reference 15:38.",
      "CH1 12:4 joins Ishmaiah and the next names (reference 12:4-5); all following verses are one lower.",
      "NEH 7:68 horses/mules has no reference counterpart; 7:69-72 correspond to reference 7:68-71. Luther 7:73 ends at settlement; the seventh-month clause starts Luther 8:1 but ends reference 7:72. Keep 7:73/8:1 as one inseparable mapping group.",
      "PSA 13:6 trust/rejoicing and 13:7 singing together comprise reference 13:6.",
      "PHP 1:16 contains selfish preaching, reference 1:17; Luther 1:17 contains loving preaching, reference 1:16. Map the reordered verses individually.",
      "REV 13:1 includes standing on the sand before the beast, reference 12:18 plus 13:1; Luther 12 ends at 17."
    ]
  },
